  "body": "I have a use case where I want to have a heading, and have a description text below it. The description text is part of the title but is is not suitable to be included in a `h2` element. The example would be:\n\n```\n<hgroup>\n  <h1>Foo</h1>\n  <p>Description of Foo</p>\n</hgroup>\n```\n\nThe text _Description of Foo_ is not a subtitle, but add contexts to the title itself. This markup is currently invalid because the `hgroup` element only allows `h1` to `h6` elements and the `template` element.\n\nA real world example could be taken from #1634:\n\n```\n<hgroup>\n  <h1 class=allcaps>HTML</h1>\n  <h2 id=living-standard class=\"no-num no-toc\">Living Standard — Last Updated <span class=pubdate>5 August 2016</span></h2>\n</hgroup>\n```\n\nHere, I don't believe the text inside `h2` could be considered to be a subtitle. It's more a description of the title itself, which is its last update date. I would feel more comfortable using a `p` element for that.\n",
